<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elizabeth II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1926">1926</a>–<a href="/years/2022">2022</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Elizabeth II was Queen of the United Kingdom from 1952 to 2022, the longest reign of any British monarch. During her reign most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s colonies became independent; several, including Tanganyika in 1961, first kept her as head of state. She was head of the Commonwealth and at her death queen of fifteen realms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elizabeth-ii.jpg" alt="Elizabeth II" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Donald McKague · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Queen_Elizabeth_II_official_portrait_for_1959_tour_(retouched)_(cropped)_(3-to-4_aspect_ratio).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…one of the best-known Pacific figures when she rode through the rain in an open carriage at the coronation of <b>Elizabeth II</b> in 1953; she was also a poet and composer, and from 1954 she chaired the Tonga Traditions Committee, which collected and recorded Tongan history and genealogies.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-tonga">Kingdom of Tonga · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>The monarchs of the period have been George V, Edward VIII, who abdicated in 1936, George VI, <b>Elizabeth II</b>, the longest-reigning British monarch from 1952 to 2022, and Charles III.</blockquote><a href="/empire/united-kingdom">United Kingdom · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>In Britain support for the monarchy reached historical lows after the death of <b>Elizabeth II</b> in 2022; in Spain a survey of 2007 found 69 per cent preferring the monarchy and 22 per cent a republic, while parties such as United Left increasingly refer to republicanism.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/republicanism">Republicanism · Legacy</a></li><li><blockquote>…obstruction or busking without a licence; in September 2022 a harmonica player who played it among the mourners for Queen <b>Elizabeth II</b> outside the British Consulate was arrested for sedition, and a year later an elderly busker was jailed for a month for playing it on the erhu.</blockquote><a href="/songs/glory-to-hong-kong">Glory to Hong Kong</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1976 Garth Henry Latta of Dunedin petitioned Parliament, and on 21 November 1977, with the consent of Queen <b>Elizabeth II</b>, Robert Muldoon's government gazetted it as New Zealand's second national anthem, equal in status with &quot;God Save the Queen&quot;.</blockquote><a href="/songs/god-defend-new-zealand">God Defend New Zealand</a></li><li><blockquote>Ralph Vaughan Williams arranged Kethe's version, with a brass fanfare and a 1621 setting by John Dowland, for the coronation of Queen <b>Elizabeth II</b> in 1953, where it was sung.</blockquote><a href="/songs/old-100th">Old 100th</a></li></ul></section>
